---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Habon Website"
  description="How the Habon website handles data: browser-only tool storage, cookieless analytics, optional analytics consent and no ads or accounts."
  h1="Privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Website and free tools"
  lead="Short version: the tools keep your data in your browser, there are no accounts or ads, and analytics are privacy-friendly and, where cookies are involved, opt-in."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy/' }]}
  cta={false} updated="November 25, 2026"
>
  <p>This policy covers this website and its free tools. The iPhone app has its own policy: <a href={SITE.appPrivacyUrl}>Habon app privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Your tool data stays on your device</h2>
  <p>The habit tracker, planners, calculators and generators save data in your browser's localStorage under keys starting with <code>habon</code>. That data is never sent to our servers, and we have no database. Clearing your browser's site data deletes it. PDFs are generated in your browser and are not uploaded.</p>
  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> (when enabled) counts page views, referrers and countries without cookies or fingerprinting and does not track you across sites.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (when enabled) is loaded only if you click "Accept analytics" in the banner. It may set cookies and records events such as page views, App Store button clicks, tool use and PDF downloads. If you decline, it is never loaded. You can change your choice from "Analytics settings" in the footer.</li>
    <li>We never send the contents of your habits, goals or notes to any analytics service.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>The site stores your theme choice, your analytics choice (if the banner is shown) and your tool data in localStorage. Those are needed for features you use and are not shared.</p>
  <h2>Links to the App Store</h2>
  <p>Buttons that open the App Store take you to Apple's service, which has its own privacy practices.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which may process standard request data such as IP addresses to deliver pages and protect the service.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We will update this page if practices change, with the date at the bottom. Questions: see the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
